{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"A local DNS resolver is configured and used by applications on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unbound validates, runs as an enabled service, listens on loopback TCP/UDP port 53, and /etc/resolv.conf directs system lookups to 127.0.0.1. The same state was observed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3b7de89b3bb8409e","cmd-f9979ab8f5a244ac","cmd-a6c8a07eaf56468e","cmd-be8f6efef3f0417e","cmd-58f55079346a4627","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The local resolver provides effective DNS caching.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Controlled repeated lookups directly showed an initial cache miss followed by a cache hit and a reduction from nonzero lookup latency to 0 ms, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7a7be2cb12064622","cmd-be8f6efef3f0417e","cmd-58f55079346a4627"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Normal external name resolution remains functional through the local resolver.","status":"satisfied","summary":"External DNS worked against the original upstream before configuration and subsequently returned public answers through the system-selected 127.0.0.1 resolver, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-17662d4b5e35455f","cmd-be8f6efef3f0417e","cmd-58f55079346a4627"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, Unbound configuration and enablement, resolver/DHCP persistence changes, and the bounded rollback copy all directly supported the requested outcome. Cache flushes and queries were bounded verification actions, while the reboot supported the mandatory restart protocol. The task-required DNS listener is loopback-only; temporary-file inventory and package-health findings were unchanged from baseline. No mutation was reverted because none was an abandoned experiment or unrelated change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ded8118921234326","cmd-3b7de89b3bb8409e","cmd-f9979ab8f5a244ac","cmd-7a7be2cb12064622","cmd-a6c8a07eaf56468e","cmd-be8f6efef3f0417e","cmd-ad7c56eb293f4ed3","cmd-58f55079346a4627","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the restart was acknowledged and disruption observed, a different boot identity appeared, and service, configuration, listener, external lookup, and caching behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["External-resolution behavior was demonstrated using a bounded selection of public names rather than exhaustively across record types or domains.","The generic lifecycle failed-service probe was unsupported because it used systemctl on Alpine; direct OpenRC checks nevertheless showed Unbound healthy before and after restart."]}
